- FlatString and JavaString are left out of the table because a program can give its own type either name. It was measured: such a program's own object answered 10 on the patch.

The transcript shows the tests failing through the harness before the code changed: at 12:06:01, on the base, before the first build ('Tests run: 5,  Failures: 3'). The generic test failed on the old code ('14', 'Tests run: 6,  Failures: 4'), and the FlatString and JavaString tests failed on aa52279ea's build before the second edit ('10', 'Tests run: 3,  Failures: 2'). After the last code edit (12:24:14) the harness gave 'OK (15 tests)'. testSystem then gave 700 tests with no failure, and testSpecData 130 with no failure, on d1228e1f0's code.

My own programs, run on the old and the new code, under walk at 1 and 4 threads and on the compiled path, confirm the repair. Calls of the library's bindings give the same values. A program's own object, object expression, functional method, or self-second operator in a program's trait is now refused at load, where before it gave a wrong value or a crash at the call. On the compiled path the checker refuses the same programs. I also checked by javap that every dotted binding the batch moves takes self first at its carrier, and that K's two CHOOSE helpers take (int, int) and (long, long). Rung F merges cleanly with this one.

My four commits change only the record:
- the worker's REPORT.md and record.md, from the run's journal;
- corrections of citations;
- row 846's moved citation as a rewrite, since the worker's note would break ledger.py's 700-character limit;
- a sentence in F-299's hand-over on a program's extender of a carried trait (row 551);
- two new rows for compiled-path defects that my programs measured, NEW-W-2 and NEW-W-3.

None changes code, none is contested, and no suite needed to run again. SKEPTIC.md is committed last, on its own, and pushed.

